      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "recto",
          "value": "\n<ol><li dir=\"ltr\">By the name of our Creator. May they build and prosper.</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">On the fifth day (of the week), the seventh day of the month of Elul, which is four thousand,\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">eight hundred and thirty-nine years [A.]M., this marriage contract [was written]</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">in the city of Tyre, which is on the coast of the [great] sea. [\u1e24alf\u014dn b.\u00a0 Aa]ron, (whose) s(oul is at) r(est), [came] and said,\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">intentionally and will[ingly ...]\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...]\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">in the manner of Jewish men, who [nou]rish, [su]stain, and [...]</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">and honor their wives faithfully. And this Gh\u0101liya [...] listened to him (accepted his proposal)\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">and consented to be married to him and to esteem and honor him, to attend and to serve [him in the manner of]\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">respectable women, the daughters of Israel, who esteem, honor, attend, and serve\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">their husbands in purity and cleanness. This Gh\u0101liya appointed her brother, \u1e24alf\u014dn b. Mus\u0101[fir],\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">to be her agent for the receipt of her qiddush (betrothal gift) from the hands of this \u1e24alf\u014dn b. Aaron.\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">And she willingly consented to all he does concerning her match and what he stipulates on behalf of her and as an obligation upon her. And there testified\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">to her two witnesses, who are acquainted with her. The mohar that this \u1e24alf\u014dn, the groom, set\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">for this Gh\u0101liya, the bride, is twelve dinars. Two dinars he gave as a first payment [...]; and there remain\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">incumbent upon him ten perfect, weighed dinars, of the dinars of the state, delayed as a debt upon him,\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">sound and firm. She has no right to claim of them one peru\u1e6da as long as he\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">is alive and she is under his jurisdiction and he fulfills her three needs. But if he hates her without\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">any misconduct (on her part) and does not fulfill her three needs, he shall pay them to her, viz. the balance of her mohar, of</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">twelve dinars, and release her with a bill of divorce. And these are what she brought with her from the Merciful and from\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">the house of her fathers: a pair of gold earrings\u20142 dinars, a wrap\u20142\u00a0 dinars, a coat made of different materials\u2014</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">\u00bc dinar, a skullcap\u20141 dinar, a skullcap and a gown\u20142 dinars, a \"half-garment\" and a slip\u2014\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">2 dinars, a wrap\u2014 1 \u00bd dinars, three \u1e6cabar\u012b cushions and a pair of \u02bfAbbad\u0101n\u012b mats\u2014\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">1 dinar, a chest and a bench\u20141 dinar, a basin and a pitcher\u20141 dinar, a lamp\u2014\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">2 dinars, and gold\u20142 dinars. The sum total is 16 dinars and \u00bd\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">dinar and \u00bc dinar. And they are for her and her son after her. And if she passes away without leaving\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">sons or daughters by him, what remains will be divided into two equal portions.\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">One portion will be acquired by her husband, and the other portion will return to the house of her fathers. And with this\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">understanding, the two sides stipulated and agreed between themselves concerning hate and love\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">and life and death and all the stipulations of the Torah and the court stipulations from beginning to end. And they took\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">upon themselves the obligation of this marriage contract according to the stringencies of all valid documents,\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">verified in court, not like promises and not like formularies. And we performed with them\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">a complete qinyan, with an implement fit for doing so, on all that is written and specified\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">above. This marriage contract is established, verified, and trustworthy wherever it is produced and read,\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">whether according to the laws of the nations of the world or according to the statutes of our lords, the sages. May they build and prosper.</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Amram ha-Kohen b. R. Aaron (may his) e(nd be) g(ood). Abraham b. R. Joshua he-\u1e25aver (who) r(ests in) E(den).\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Japheth b. Abraham b. Siman-Tav (may his) e(nd be)g(ood). Samuel b. R. Nathan m(ay his) s(oul be) b(ound) i(n the bundle of) l(ife).</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Amram he-\u1e25aver b. \u1e62edaqa (who) r(ests in) E(den).\u00a0 </li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
